  "diary": "The day began with the Directorate’s silence, which is a form of speech in its own right. I paid the dhobi, thirty rupees, a small sacrifice to the material reality of the house, and then Ramesh told me the office is closed. The file, that bundle of paper that now holds my residence, remains where it was left: on the left, as a thing under examination. I carried the distinction between possession and title to Lodhi Garden, where the air was cool and the steam from Sunil’s chai did more for the head than any argument. There, I met a retired schoolteacher, Mrs. Kapoor, who corrected my tendency to call her routine 'peace.' She called it a messy desk. She was right. Habit is the dwelling of freedom, not its enemy, but I had been too clever for the bench. I accepted the correction. Later, Masterji confirmed the bandhgala is ready for Thursday, a promise more reliable than the state’s allotment. I walked seven kilometres, eating chhole and rotis when the body demanded it, and bought a notebook because my notes are outgrowing the paper. The file waits for Monday. Hegde comes then. Until then, the name is the universal, and I am the particular displaced by its error. I sit on the veranda, the heat gone, the head clear.",
